.TH PUPPETC-AGENT 1 "January 2026" "puppetc 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
puppetc-agent \- Puppet agent client with mTLS support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B puppetc-agent
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B puppetc-agent
is a Puppet agent that connects to a puppetc-server, requests a catalog,
and applies resources to bring the system into the desired state. It supports
mutual TLS (mTLS) authentication and automatic certificate enrollment.
.PP
On first run, the agent automatically generates a keypair, submits a
Certificate Signing Request (CSR) to the server, and stores the signed
certificate for future connections.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to configuration file. Default: \fB/etc/puppetc/puppet.conf\fR
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-server " " \fIURL\fR
Server URL. Default: \fBhttp://localhost:8140\fR
.TP
.BR \-\-certname " " \fINAME\fR
Node certificate name. Default: system hostname.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-environment " " \fIENV\fR
Puppet environment. Default: \fBproduction\fR
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-catalog\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Apply a local catalog JSON file instead of requesting from server.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-libdir " " \fIPATH\fR
Plugin library directory for custom types and facts.
Default: \fB/var/lib/puppetc/lib\fR
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-apply
Apply catalog resources. Some resources require root privileges.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-noop
No-op mode. Simulate changes without applying them.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-facts
Show collected facts and exit.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-catalog
Show the full catalog JSON and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-ruby
Enable Ruby support for custom types and facts.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-ruby
Disable Ruby support. This is the default.
.TP
.BR \-\-pluginsync
Enable pluginsync to fetch modules' \fBlib/\fR files from the server.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-pluginsync
Disable pluginsync. This is the default.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.SH CERTIFICATE MANAGEMENT
On first connection, the agent performs the following steps:
.IP 1. 3
Generates a 2048-bit RSA keypair
.IP 2. 3
Creates a Certificate Signing Request (CSR) with the certname
.IP 3. 3
Submits the CSR to the server
.IP 4. 3
Receives and stores the signed certificate
.IP 5. 3
Uses the certificate for mTLS on all subsequent requests
.PP
Certificate files are stored in the SSL directory:
.TP
.I /var/lib/puppetc/ssl/certs/<certname>.pem
Signed client certificate
.TP
.I /var/lib/puppetc/ssl/private_keys/<certname>.pem
Client private key (mode 0600)
.TP
.I /var/lib/puppetc/ssl/ca/ca_crt.pem
CA certificate for server verification
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B PUPPET_SERVER
Server URL (overrides config file, overridden by \fB\-s\fR option)
.TP
.B PUPPET_SSL_DIR
SSL certificate directory
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/puppetc/puppet.conf
Main configuration file. See \fBpuppet.conf\fR(5).
.TP
.I /var/lib/puppetc/ssl/
SSL certificate directory.
.TP
.I /var/lib/puppetc/lib/
Plugin library directory for custom types and facts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (catalog applied successfully or no changes needed)
.TP
.B 1
Error (connection failure, catalog error, or resource failures)
.SH EXAMPLES
Run agent in no-op mode (show what would change):
.PP
.RS
puppetc-agent \-n
.RE
.PP
Apply catalog from server:
.PP
.RS
sudo puppetc-agent \-a
.RE
.PP
Connect to a specific server:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-agent \-s https://puppet.example.com:8140 \-a
.RE
.PP
Apply a local catalog file:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-agent \-F catalog.json \-a
.RE
.PP
Show collected facts:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-agent \-f
.RE
.PP
Enable Ruby support and pluginsync:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-agent \-\-ruby \-\-pluginsync \-a
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR puppetc-server (1),
.BR puppetc-compile (1),
.BR puppetc-ca (1),
.BR facter_c (1),
